  "s5": {
    "duration": 21.125,
    "text": "Each row of the detector sees the crystal from a slightly different angle, and rings at its own frequency. On a GPU, x Ray fits every row. In this module, you'll fit one trace whose answer you know, find out how a mode can go missing, and fit a whole detector. A fit always returns modes. The question is whether they're all there.",
